Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports** (from 427 exported rows after deduplicating overlapping export pages).

**Merged as one issue, split into two causes (`parser` and `hint`, plus 5 `oneDayMove` reports filed under `parser`).** Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put multiple problems into `#4471`:

1. **[#1 · `parser`](https://github.com/olafkrawczyk/support-kb-4471/issues/1)** (**fixed** — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`) — **379** reports under `causeOf() === 'parser'` in `causes.ts` (**374** month/day-swap reports plus **5** `oneDayMove` reports) across all 11 day-first (`DD/MM`) tenants on `app` (204), `email` (150), and `booking-v2` `form` (25, `DD/MM/YYYY` hint), seen `2026-04-01` → `2026-10-04`.
2. **[#2 · `hint`](https://github.com/olafkrawczyk/support-kb-4471/issues/2)** (**won't fix** — `booking-v3 form retired`) — **33** reports on the `form` channel across the 3 tenants on `booking-v3` (`alder.physio` ×12, `copper.studio` ×11, `pale.harbour` ×10), seen `2026-04-17` → `2026-09-22`. `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so customers type month first while the form parses day first (`DD/MM`).
3. **[#3 · `oneDayMove`](https://github.com/olafkrawczyk/support-kb-4471/issues/3)** — **5** reports (`R-41202`, `R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, `R-41620`) across 5 tenants (`kettle.books`, `alder.physio`, `nine.lanterns`, `pale.harbour`, `lantern.row`), seen `2026-04-02` → `2026-10-04`, read as a one-day move and filed under `parser` by tenant.

<Callout>
Resolved 05 Oct (#4471 closed): parser fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales), hint won't fix (booking-v3 form retired).
</Callout>

